


DMESG(1)            UNIX Programmer's Manual               DMESG(1)



NAME
     dmesg - print the kernel log

SYNOPSIS
     dmesg

DESCRIPTION
     _D_m_e_s_g prints the contents of the kernel log ring buffer:
     boot messages, module loads, device registrations, and any
     kernel diagnostics since boot (up to the 4 KB the ring
     holds; older messages scroll off).

     This is an FGX-native tool: the kernel exposes the ring
     directly through a system call, so there is no /dev/kmem
     spelunking and no incremental (-) mode -- the whole ring
     prints every time.

SEE ALSO
     stat(1), uptime(1)

